{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42742452 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42742452 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42742452","source":"MED","pmid":"42742452","pmcid":"PMC13576935","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13576935"]},"doi":"10.1002/iid3.70523","title":"Gut Microbiota Dysbiosis Mediates &lt;sup&gt;125&lt;/sup&gt;I-Induced Radiation Colitis via Host Transcriptional Regulation.","authorString":"Liu P, Zeng X, Liu W, Xie H, Fang Y, Yang E, Tang X, Fan C, Chen Y.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Liu P","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Pingping","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Imaging, Sichuan Corps Hospital of PAP, Leshan, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zeng X","lastName":"Zeng","firstName":"Xiong","initials":"X","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-9013-7603"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, Xinqiao Hospital, Army Medical University, Chongqing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu W","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Wenjing","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, The First Mobile Corps Hospital of PAP, Dingzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Xie H","lastName":"Xie","firstName":"Huichao","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, Xinqiao Hospital, Army Medical University, Chongqing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Fang Y","lastName":"Fang","firstName":"Yongkun","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Imaging, Sichuan Corps Hospital of PAP, Leshan, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yang E","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Erwan","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, The First Mobile Corps Hospital of PAP, Dingzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Tang X","lastName":"Tang","firstName":"Xiaoqi","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Laboratory Medicine, The First Medical Center of Chinese PLA General Hospital, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Fan C","lastName":"Fan","firstName":"Chenglin","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Imaging, Sichuan Corps Hospital of PAP, Leshan, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Chen Y","lastName":"Chen","firstName":"Yihui","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9392-7144"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, Xinqiao Hospital, Army Medical University, Chongqing, China."},{"affiliation":"Department of General Surgery, The First Mobile Corps Hospital of PAP, Dingzhou, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9392-7144"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-9013-7603"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"9","volume":"14","journalIssueId":4259497,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Immun Inflamm Dis","title":"Immunity, inflammation and disease","essn":"2050-4527","issn":"2050-4527","nlmid":"101635460","isoabbreviation":"Immun Inflamm Dis"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e70523","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Iodine-125 (<sup>125</sup>I) seed therapy is recognized for treating abdominal solid tumors with minimal adjacent tissue damage but may induce radiation colitis when its implantation near colonic tissues, leading to a poor prognosis. Nevertheless, the underlying pathogenesis is not well understood.<h4>Objective</h4>This research aims to investigate the role of gut microbiota and host immune-transcriptional responses in the pathogenesis of <sup>125</sup>I-induced radiation colitis.<h4>Methods</h4>We implanted <sup>125</sup>I seeds intraperitoneally in mice and assessed colonic damage via histology, TUNEL staining, cytokine assays, and tight‑junction protein measurements. Fecal microbiota were profiled by 16S rRNA sequencing, and colonic transcriptomes by RNA‑seq. Multi‑omics integration (Spearman correlation, KEGG, RDA, Procrustes) was used to link microbial taxa, differentially expressed genes, and pathological features.<h4>Results</h4><sup>125</sup>I exposure caused mucosal necrosis, lowered ZO-1 and occludin levels, and raised IL-1α, IL-1β, IL-6, and TNF-α. 16S rRNA sequencing revealed altered microbial β-diversity and dysbiosis, characterized by reduced Lachnospiraceae, Mucispirillum, and Desulfovibrio, and increased Clostridium methylpentosum and Bifidobacterium. RNA-seq analysis revealed differentially expressed genes such as Angptl7, Apoh, C7, and Ccl7. Integrated analyses, including Spearman correlation, KEGG enrichment, redundancy analysis, and Procrustes analysis, confirmed strong associations between certain microbes, host gene expression, and pathological phenotypes.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Our findings indicate that <sup>125</sup>I irradiation is associated with gut dysbiosis and concurrent host immune‑transcriptional reprogramming, which may jointly contribute to radiation colitis. Although these results lay a foundation for microbiota‑targeted interventions, the causative role of microbial changes remains to be confirmed by functional experiments.","affiliation":"Department of Medical Imaging, Sichuan Corps Hospital of PAP, Leshan, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China.","grantId":"82500678","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Colon","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MI","qualifierName":"microbiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"RE","qualifierName":"radiation effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Inbred C57BL"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Colitis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ET","qualifierName":"etiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MI","qualifierName":"microbiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Radiation Injuries, Experimental","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ET","qualifierName":"etiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MI","qualifierName":"microbiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Iodine Radioisotopes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"RNA, Ribosomal, 16S","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cytokines","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Expression Regulation","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"RE","qualifierName":"radiation effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Dysbiosis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MI","qualifierName":"microbiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gastrointestinal Microbiome","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"RE","qualifierName":"radiation effects"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Microbial Dysbiosis","Radiation Colitis","Iodine‐125 (125I) Seed Therapy"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Iodine Radioisotopes","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"RNA, Ribosomal, 16S","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Cytokines","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Iodine-125","registryNumber":"GVO776611R"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/iid3.70523"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13576935"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13576935?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-09-15","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-15","dateOfRevision":"2026-09-17","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-01","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-16","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-16","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}